2. Mottled with black and yellow: as, a ''tortoise-shell'' cat or butterfly. {{smaller|The cat of this name is a mere color-variety of the domestic animal; the insect is a vanessoid, as ''Vanessa urticæ'' or ''V. polychlora.''—'''Tortoise-shell goose.''' See ''goose.''—'''Tortoise-shell tiger.''' See ''tiger.''—'''Tortoise-shell ware,''' a fine pottery colored with oxid of copper and manganese so that the color penetrates the paste itself, producing a certain resemblance to the marking of tortoise-shell.}}

